  "hints": [
    "Every keystroke is a request, and most prefixes are popular. What answers repeated lookups in a millisecond?",
    "Cache misses need an index that can find completions for a prefix quickly.",
    "LB (2) \u2192 Suggest API (30) \u2192 Prefix Cache (2 \u00d7 32 GB) \u2192 Elasticsearch (3). Connect the cache to the index so misses fall through to it."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 2800
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Autocomplete is a prefix lookup. A trie (or an index with edge n-grams) maps each prefix to its top-k completions.",
    "Because a few prefixes dominate, caching the top results per prefix absorbs almost all traffic.",
    "Clients also debounce keystrokes (wait ~100 ms) and cache results locally, which cuts server load further."
  ]
